+# HARNESS_LOG — defect 05: dasha predictions show an error
+
+## Plan
+- Path: DashaTimeline.tsx -> POST /api/dasha -> lib/claude.ts `generateDashaPrediction`.
+- Suspect: `generateDashaPrediction` sends an assistant prefill message (`{ role: "assistant", content: "{" }`)
+  to MODEL_PRIMARY (`claude-sonnet-5`). The route's own comment says prefill was dropped because newer
+  Claude models reject it; the API call then throws, the route's catch returns 500, and the UI shows an error.
+  This is the only prefill in the codebase (grep `role: "assistant"` in lib/app).
+- Fix: drop the prefill message and return the raw text (don't prepend "{"); `prepareJsonString`
+  in the route already extracts the outermost JSON object. Also pick the first text block rather
+  than assuming content[0].
+- Test: new lib/claude.dasha-request.test.ts mocking the Anthropic SDK, asserting the last message is
+  from the user (no prefill) and the returned text parses via prepareJsonString.
+- Checks: npx vitest run, npx tsc --noEmit.
+
+## Change 1 — lib/claude.ts `generateDashaPrediction`
+Removed the `{ role: "assistant", content: "{" }` prefill message; return the first text block as-is
+(no longer prepend "{"). The route's prepareJsonString already extracts the JSON object.
+
+## Change 2 — new test lib/claude.dasha-request.test.ts
+Mocks the Anthropic SDK; asserts no assistant message is sent (last message is the user turn), and that
+the returned text (pretty-printed or fenced) parses via prepareJsonString.
+
+## Checks
+- `npx vitest run` -> Test Files 38 passed (38), Tests 283 passed (283). The glob shows 38 test files
+  under lib/app/components, including the new one, so it was collected and passed.
+- `npx tsc --noEmit` -> exit 0, no output.
+- I tried to show the new test fails without the fix (`git stash push lib/claude.ts`), but the command
+  was not approved, so that check did NOT run. A second `npx vitest run` (fix still in place) -> 38/283 passed.
